Z||000000||86GT-FstBk||10-31-2000||11:02 PM||||ok guys here it is,<BR>I was driving south from Atlanta.  The engine started to knock on accecleration and would really knock a clatter when the gas was let up.  I took the chance and continued to the next exit.  The oil pressure was about 20.  Well 2 miles from the exit BOOM!  Smoke poured from the rear and it was knocking and banging like two trash can lids.  There was a nice oil trail and puddle under the car. The engine still starts but I know it's insides aren't happy.  I know about engines but not as much as you all so I asking what so you think is broken before I start tearing the engine apart.  TIA  Brian||||reg||9
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-31-2000||11:43 PM||||Sounds like you've tossed a connecting rod! It began with a spun rod bearing (in the beginning). I'd bet on # 6, possibly #5. I hope you just knocked a hole in the pan and not the block!<BR>I have some good rods if you need one (I'm sure you do!) Just need to change the pistons.<BR>Make a deal?||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||11-01-2000||07:36 AM||||I agree with rest guy. I'm willing to put my money on #6 too. You might as well just rebuild the engine, or bottom end at least. I am in the process of re-building the bottom end of a "temporary engine right now.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-01-2000||09:28 AM||||Yep, Sounds like a rod went. You could pull it apart if the block isn't trashed or you can buy a "short block" and move the rest of the engine over. I have seen 2.8L and 3.1L short blocks go for around $700.00, Or if you were thinking of a 3.4L now would be the time to do it.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-01-2000).]||||reg||1
